--   Upgrades the Chat04 expected original Levy compensated C2 negative-jump theorem to integrability of the literal discounted stopped Taylor kernel on the individual intrinsic source jump counting measure NX(ω), for P-almost every original source sample path. Its only source intensity hypotheses are the explicit right-cont future-rectangle identity hFuture and exact physical μ clock hμclock; the proof uses predictable C2 jump kernel measurability, true-source bounded signed product L1 against μ×X.ν, sigma-finite predictable marked measure uniqueness and a previously proved original source fibre integrability theorem. Both the real source positive-time marks and inclusive ruinTime are literal.
